### Key Observations & Data-Integrity Notes

- **Combined ratio reconciliation verified**: 95.33% = Claims ratio (65.00%, Net Incurred Claims/NEP) + Expense ratio (30.33%, EoM/NWP) — matches the company's own stated formula in Annexure 3, confirming internal consistency of the extracted figures.
- **NEP sourcing rationale**: Since Star Health writes business only in the Miscellaneous (Health + Personal Accident) segment (Fire/Marine lines are NIL), the Schedule 1D "Premium Earned (Net)" figure of ₹11,261.59 cr represents the company-wide statutory NEP, not a segment-only number.
- **PAT swung sharply to profit**: FY23 PAT of ₹618.59 cr marks a strong turnaround from a **loss of ₹(1,040.67) cr in FY22**, driven by normalization of COVID-related claims and a large ESOP-driven deferred tax impact (₹207.81 cr deferred tax charge in FY23 vs a ₹346.95 cr deferred tax **credit** in FY22).
- **Solvency strengthened materially**: Solvency ratio improved from 1.67x (FY22) to 2.14x (FY23), comfortably above the IRDAI-prescribed 1.50x minimum, reflecting capital infusion (₹27.71 cr share premium addition) and the return to profitability.
- **Auditors' opinion**: An unmodified/unqualified opinion was issued jointly by Brahmayya & Co. and V. Sankar Aiyar & Co., dated **28 April 2023** — used consistently as the filing date across all rows above.</ans>
